# Architecture

## Runtime topology

```
Browser ──► Next.js on Vercel (frontend/)     auth, editor, RLS-covered Supabase I/O
              │
              └── Bearer JWT ──► FastAPI (backend/)
                    local: uvicorn :8000 (JOB_DISPATCH_MODE=background)
                    prod:  API Gateway → API Lambda → async worker Lambda
                                    │
                                    └── service role ──► Storage (sketches read only)
                                    └── user JWT client ──► Postgres (RLS)

Respondent ──► /f/[slug] ──► public_forms view (anon SELECT)
              ├── INSERT form_responses (published forms only)
              └── file_upload ──► response-uploads bucket (anon INSERT, owner signed URLs)
```

- **Frontend** owns auth (`@supabase/ssr` httpOnly cookies), form CRUD, responses UI, and anything PostgREST RLS already allows. Calls FastAPI via `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` (`src/lib/api/forms.ts`).
- **Backend** owns `POST /forms/generate`, job polling, `POST /forms/validate`. Images are never uploaded to FastAPI — only `storage_path` in JSON; backend downloads via service role. Production jobs run on the **worker Lambda** (`JOB_DISPATCH_MODE=lambda`).
- **Supabase** owns schema, RLS, triggers, and private buckets `sketches` + `response-uploads`.

See `.cursor/rules/deployment.mdc` for Vercel + Lambda details.

## LangGraph pipeline

Path: `backend/app/pipeline/nodes/`

```
preprocess → vision_extract → structure → validate
                              ↓ (if invalid & repairs left)
                         repair → vision_extract (once)
                              ↓
                           persist
```

- `MAX_REPAIRS = 1` in `pipeline/graph.py`.
- Hard failures: raise (job → `failed`).
- Soft failures: append to `state["warnings"]`, continue; `needs_review` on low-confidence fields in `definition`.
- Contract: `backend/app/schemas/definition.py` (`Definition` Pydantic model) ↔ `forms.definition` JSON.

## Frontend structure (`frontend/src/`)

| Area | Path | Notes |
|------|------|-------|
| Auth pages | `app/(auth)/` | login, signup, forgot-password |
| App shell | `app/(app)/` | sidebar: home, drafts, published, create, responses |
| Drafts | `app/(app)/forms/drafts/` | owner draft forms (`deleted_at` null) |
| Trash | `app/(app)/forms/trash/` | soft-deleted drafts; 1-day retention |
| Published | `app/(app)/forms/published/` | published forms + share links |
| Responses | `app/(app)/forms/responses/` | response picker + sheet (CSV export) |
| Public forms | `app/f/[slug]/` | no internal `id` in UI |
| Auth callback | `app/auth/callback/route.ts` | code exchange |
| Session gate | `src/proxy.ts` exports `proxy` | **Not** `middleware.ts` |
| Supabase | `lib/supabase/{client,server,proxy}.ts` | browser vs server vs session refresh |
| UI primitives | `components/ui/` | Base UI `render={...}` slot pattern |

Read `frontend/node_modules/next/dist/docs/` for Next.js 16 APIs before changing routing or data fetching.

## Backend structure (`backend/app/`)

| Module | Responsibility |
|--------|----------------|
| `main.py` | CORS, `/api/v1` routers, lifespan logging |
| `config.py` | `get_settings()` only — `@lru_cache`, never raw `Settings()` |
| `security.py` | JWKS-first JWT (`CurrentUser` dependency) |
| `supabase_client.py` | `get_user_client(jwt)` vs `get_service_client()` |
| `jobs.py` | `run_generation_job`; `dispatch_to_lambda` when `JOB_DISPATCH_MODE=lambda` |
| `observability.py` | Optional Langfuse client; traces grouped per generation job |
| `lambda_handlers.py` | `api_handler` (Mangum), `worker_handler` — AWS only |
| `routers/` | Thin routers; register in `main.create_app()` |
| `pipeline/` | LangGraph state + graph + nodes |
| `schemas/` | `definition.py` (contract), `api.py` (HTTP shapes) |

## Database (Supabase)

Tables: `profiles`, `forms`, `form_responses`, `generation_jobs`. View: `public_forms` (published rows only).

Storage path invariants:

```
sketches/{auth.uid()}/{form_id_or_filename}.{ext}           # owner sketch uploads
response-uploads/{form_id}/{uuid}.{ext}                   # respondent file_upload answers
```

`file_upload` answers in `form_responses.answers`: `{ path, name, size, mime }`. Helpers: `frontend/src/lib/storage/response-uploads.ts`.

## API surface (backend)

- `GET /api/v1/health`
- `GET /api/v1/me`
- `POST /api/v1/forms/generate` — `{ storage_path, form_id? }`
- `GET /api/v1/forms/generate/{job_id}`
- `POST /api/v1/forms/validate`

## Change discipline

- Minimize scope; match existing patterns in the tree you touch.
- Cross-cutting schema/security changes: migration + types regen + update `public_forms` if respondents need new data.
